{
  "requirement": "The repository MUST be a Cargo workspace containing the `habeas` package at the repository root and the `habeas-sdk` package in `crates/habeas-sdk/`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed test is adequate for `requirements.layout.project.workspace`. It is `tests/repository.rs#fn[workspace_contains_frontend_and_sdk_but_not_the_vendor_fork]`, and it is marked {test} for the requirement.\n\nThe requirement has three obligations: the repository is a Cargo workspace, the `habeas` package is at the repository root, and the `habeas-sdk` package is in `crates/habeas-sdk/`.\n\n- **Workspace and membership.** The test runs `cargo metadata --offline --locked --no-deps` from `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR`. It asserts that the command succeeds and that the `workspace_members` names include both `habeas` and `habeas-sdk`. The test also requires several `habeas-language*` crates to be members. Those are path dependencies, and Cargo treats a path dependency as a workspace member only when a `[workspace]` section exists. So the test implicitly confirms that the root is a real workspace and not a single package.\n- **`habeas` at the root.** The metadata command runs in the manifest directory of the crate that owns the test. The test then indexes `repository_toml(\"Cargo.toml\")[\"dependencies\"]`, so the root manifest is a real package manifest and not a virtual one. Together with the `habeas` name assertion, this confirms the root package.\n- **`habeas-sdk` in `crates/habeas-sdk/`.** The test asserts that `crates/habeas-sdk/src/lib.rs` exists. It also asserts that the root manifest's `habeas-sdk` dependency has `path = \"crates/habeas-sdk\"`. Cargo requires the package at a dependency path to carry the dependency's name, so a package named `habeas-sdk` must sit at that location.\n\nThe test does not compare the SDK package's `manifest_path` directly. A violating layout would have to pass every check above, and that is implausible. For example, a second `habeas-sdk` package elsewhere in the workspace would still leave the path dependency pointing at `crates/habeas-sdk`.\n\nThe negative assertion on `habeas-rig` is outside this requirement. No acknowledgments or {fixme} references apply.",
